{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>See, HaShem has called.</b> What is the meaning of 'see'? Because when Moses said to Israel that Bezalel would make the Tabernacle, Israel were murmuring after Moses and saying that he takes all the greatness for himself and for his family. Moses said to them: Know and see, that I do not act of my own mind but by command of the Holy One, blessed be He. And even Moses himself, at the hour when the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke to him concerning the work of the Tabernacle — ״ועשית״ — assumed he would do it all. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Not as you think, but a righteous man who was killed on account of the sin of the Calf — that is, Hur — let his grandson come and make it, because the Tabernacle was an atonement for that deed. And this is what the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״ראה קראתי״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:47.859157391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}